# 1.3.intake.gaps.stone

## .what

name the **knowledge gaps** — the facts not yet known that would change the read (an absent
temperature, an unconfirmed dose, an unreported prior episode). these feed the assay phase, which
orders tests to close them.

## .inputs

- `1.2.intake.structure.yield.md` — the structured timeline + entities

## .do

- list each unknown that would shift a scenario's plausibility or severity
- mark which are cheap to close (ask the owner) vs need a test (feeds phase 4)
- do NOT guess the absent value — a gap is a gap until closed (`absence-of-evidence`)

## .emit

into `1.3.intake.gaps.yield.md`.

## .done when

the knowledge gaps are listed, each tagged cheap-to-close vs test-needed, none filled by guess.
